  "notes": "The biggest post-Idol country voice — arena country-pop with rock guitars and \"drivetime drums.\" Three facts here are documented outright and none of them is inferred: the catalogue is \"unusually minor-heavy for radio country — F♯ minor, A minor, C minor, F minor and E♭ minor all appear on singles alongside the major-key ballads,\" which is the minor-weighted key set; the signature single is \"in F♯ minor … progression F♯m–E–Dsus2–C♯ = i–VII–VI–V (a major-quality V from harmonic minor),\" which is the top family and the harmonic_minor scale weight; and the vocal range is \"F♯3–C♯5,\" MIDI 54–73, which is the melody register floor and the anchor for the belt above it. The drum grammar is quoted — \"hats/cross-stick verse, big backbeat from the chorus, half-time bridge, final chorus with tom doubling\" — and the 2018 record's \"innovative overhead mic techniques\" is authored as an overhead-forward, roomy kit rather than as a mic. The widest dynamic range in the section is a documented engineering problem (\"she can literally go from singing very softly to blowing the microphone out\"), so `velocityVar` is the highest in this batch and the accent tier runs to the ceiling. ⚠ Boundary flag: \"Before He Cheats\" is documented as a shuffle in cut time and that groove belongs to `country-shuffle`; the artist stays here. ⚠ The catalogue tempo readings fold songdata's 137–160 figures and carry the section's [LOW-CONF] class mark. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the perc lane set and density, the counter ratio and the arrangement section lengths.",
